    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` response is built by `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, mapping an `Owner` entity to the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`. I added an `initials` field there, mirroring how the existing `displayName` field is handled:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (which drives generation of `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `initials`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\",\n       expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n   This upper-cases the first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot \u2014 e.g. `\"john\"` / `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`.\n\n## Result\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes and the build reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
